---
<ProductLayout title={page.title} hreflang={hreflang} description={page.description} canonical={page.canonical} ogImage="/images/flaxseed-kernels.jpg" gallery={gallery} category={category} price={price} related={related} descriptionHtml={`<p><span>The Hulled Flaxseed manufacturer is located in Inner Mongolia, China. Flaxseeds are locally selected fine seeds.</span></p><h2><strong>Product Description: Hulled Flaxseed</strong></h2><h3><strong>Product Overview</strong></h3><p>Hulled Flaxseed is derived from flaxseeds through a meticulous dehulling process that removes the outer shell while preserving the nutrient-rich core. Compared to whole flaxseeds, flaxseed kernels are easier to digest and process, making them ideal for direct consumption and industrial applications.</p><h3><strong>Dehulling Process</strong></h3><p>Our Hulled Flaxseed is produced using advanced physical dehulling techniques, which include:</p><ol><li><strong>Cleaning &amp; Screening</strong> – Removing impurities through air separation, sieving, and gravity separation.</li><li><strong>Low-Temperature Dehulling</strong> – Utilizing mechanical dehulling under controlled temperatures to retain maximum nutrients.</li><li><strong>Separation &amp; Sorting</strong> – Using airflow separation and fine screening to ensure complete removal of hulls and improve purity.</li><li><strong>Color Sorting &amp; Inspection</strong> – Advanced color sorting machines remove discolored or broken kernels, ensuring consistent quality.</li></ol><h2><strong>Nutritional Information (Per 100g)</strong></h2><table border="1" cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0"><tbody><tr><td width="257">Nutrient</td><td width="170">Amount</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Energy</td><td width="170">534 kcal</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Protein</td><td width="170">18.3 g</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Fat</td><td width="170">42.2 g</td></tr><tr><td width="257">– Including α-Linolenic Acid (Omega-3)</td><td width="170">22.8 g</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Carbohydrates</td><td width="170">28.9 g</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Dietary Fiber</td><td width="170">27.3 g</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Vitamin B1 (Thiamine)</td><td width="170">1.6 mg</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Vitamin B6</td><td width="170">0.47 mg</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Folate</td><td width="170">87 μg</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Magnesium</td><td width="170">392 mg</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Calcium</td><td width="170">255 mg</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Potassium</td><td width="170">813 mg</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Iron</td><td width="170">5.7 mg</td></tr><tr><td width="257">Zinc</td><td width="170">4.3 mg</td></tr></tbody></table><h2><strong>Applications &amp; Benefits Compared to Whole Flaxseeds</strong></h2><p>Flaxseed kernels are widely used in food, nutraceutical, and pet food industries. Compared to whole flaxseeds, they offer the following advantages:</p><table border="1" cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0"><thead><tr><th>Application</th><th>Whole Flaxseeds</th><th>Flaxseed Kernels</th><th>Key Benefits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Baking (Bread, Cakes, Cookies)</strong></td><td>Require grinding or pre-treatment for better texture</td><td>Can be added directly for enhanced texture and nutrition</td><td>Better flavor, reduced processing steps</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Beverages (Smoothies, Plant-based Milk)</strong></td><td>Need soaking and straining</td><td>Mixes easily and dissolves better</td><td>Smoother texture, no need for filtering</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Dietary Supplements (Oatmeal, Salads)</strong></td><td>Hard shells may affect digestion and texture</td><td>Ready to eat and easier to digest</td><td>Improved absorption</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Functional Foods (Protein Bars, Energy Bars)</strong></td><td>Affects texture and consistency</td><td>Blends seamlessly with other ingredients</td><td>Ideal for premium nutrition products</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pet Food</strong></td><td>Requires crushing for digestibility</td><td>Easily mixed for improved Omega-3 intake</td><td>Supports pet coat and skin health</td></tr></tbody></table><h4><strong>Packaging &amp; OEM Customization</strong></h4><ul><li><strong>Standard Packaging</strong>: 25kg bags (food-grade kraft paper bags/PP woven bags with PE inner lining)</li><li><strong>Custom Small Packaging</strong>: Available in 250g, 500g, 1kg, and other sizes for retail markets</li><li><strong>OEM/ODM Orders</strong>: We offer private labeling, customized specifications, and tailored blends. Global partners are welcome to collaborate!</li></ul><h2><strong>FAQ (Frequently Asked Questions)</strong></h2><p><strong>1. How should flaxseed kernels be stored?</strong><br/>Flaxseed kernels should be stored in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight. For long-term freshness, refrigeration is recommended to prevent oxidation.</p><p><strong>2. Do flaxseed kernels have the same health benefits as whole flaxseeds?</strong><br/>Yes! Flaxseed kernels retain the same essential nutrients, including Omega-3 fatty acids, protein, and fiber, but are easier to digest due to the removal of the hard outer shell.</p><p><strong>3. Can flaxseed kernels be consumed raw?</strong><br/>Yes, flaxseed kernels can be eaten raw or added to various foods like yogurt, smoothies, and baked goods. Unlike whole flaxseeds, they do not need to be ground for nutrient absorption.</p><p><strong>4. Are flaxseed kernels suitable for gluten-free diets?</strong><br/>Yes, flaxseed kernels are naturally gluten-free and an excellent source of plant-based nutrients for gluten-free diets.</p><p><strong>5. Do you offer private labeling and bulk orders?</strong><br/>Yes, we provide OEM and ODM services, including private labeling, bulk packaging, and customized formulations to meet different business needs.</p>`} />
